# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "Under an inline parser mode no block rule stands"

# The parsermode pragma sets parseAsInline for the whole tiddler, so TiddlyWiki parses one
# inline run and every block marker after it yields plain text. Measured: a heading marker
# and a list marker come back as a single text node.

! Under block mode a heading builds

\parsermode block
! A heading here
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.heading.heading-1.tiddlywiki5 markup.heading.punctuation.definition.tiddlywiki5

! Under inline mode the same marker reads as content

\parsermode inline
! Not a heading here
#<- - markup.heading.punctuation.definition.tiddlywiki5
#<- - meta.heading.heading-1.tiddlywiki5
* Not a list item
#<- - punctuation.definition.unnumbered.unordered.ul.li.list.markup.tiddlywiki5

And an inline construct still reads: [[A Link]] here
#                                    ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.link.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.link.outer.begin.tiddlywiki5

